    "created_at": "2016-12-09T00:43:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-09T00:43:07Z",
    "body": "> Following the logic, in those certain cases, whatever is not a character reference constitutes valid text (unless explicitly prohibited for other reasons).\r\n\r\nNo, this doesn't follow.\r\n\r\n> Either text should be prohibited from containing those kinds of strings in all contexts that allow character references\r\n\r\nThis is already the case: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#elements-2:syntax-ambiguous-ampersand\r\n\r\nClosing since I believe this is already covered in the spec, but happy to continue discussing, and reopen if I missed something.",
