    "body": "I think you're missing something. 😉\r\n\r\nAmbiguous ampersand disallows `&asdfasdf;`. But it does not cover `&#x3aXYZ` (no semicolon).  That string is also not covered by \"character references\" definition since it requires the trailing semicolon.\r\n\r\nI think \"character references\" should be changed as follows:\r\n\r\n* Named character references: Add \"if the name is one that is not terminated by a U+003B SEMICOLON character (;), then this is a character reference that must not be used.\"\r\n* Decimal numeric character reference: Add \"If the U+003B SEMICOLON character (;) is omitted, and the next character is any other non-ASCII digit character, or there is no next character, then this is a character reference that must not be used.\"\r\n* Hexadecimal numeric character reference: Add \"\"If the U+003B SEMICOLON character (;) is omitted, and the next character is any other non-ASCII hex digit character, or there is no next character, then this is a character reference that must not be used.\"\r\n\r\nExcept named character references are more complex - need to check the next character there also, and the parser's behavior is different in attributes and in content...",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
