    "updated_at": "2016-12-11T21:46:23Z",
    "body": "The \"Writing\" section is intended to be pedantically correct (where correct means matching the parser section), but only cover how to write conforming documents. It does intentionally not cover non-conforming cases (e.g. no optional end tags for non-conforming elements; void elements only includes conforming elements). But I don't see a problem in principle in saying \"foo is a character reference\" and then only a subset of those are conforming.\r\n\r\nI would also be open to fiddling with the definition of ambiguous ampersand, if as a result of doing the above the ambiguous ampersand thing can be simplified/changed to only cover cases that are not character references...\r\n\r\nIf you are interested in working on this in form of a pull request, that would be very welcome and I am happy to guide you. Otherwise I will get to this eventually. 🙂",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
